 "result_text": "I added `\"swimlane\"` to `UserStory.allowed_params` in `taiga/models/models.py`. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a Taiga server.\n\n`update()` only sends the fields listed in `allowed_params`, and `swimlane` wasn't one of them. The story's swimlane was never in the PUT payload, so Taiga reset it to Unclassified whenever you changed the status. That also explains why `story.swimlane = <id>` had no effect, while `None` appeared to work: it was just the unclassified default.\n\nWith the field included, `story.update()` sends the current swimlane back unchanged, and assigning a swimlane id should now take effect.\n\nI didn't update the `UserStory` docstring's `:param` list, which still doesn't mention `swimlane`.",
